### useAuth() hook
```ts
const { activeAccount, accounts, signIn, signOut, switchAccount } = useAuth();
```

### Session behavior
- In-memory only (resets on page refresh — F-17)
- No localStorage or cookies
- Calendar events are shared across all accounts (per-account isolation is out of scope)

## Routing

- `/sign-in` → `<SignInPage />` — shown when no active account
- `/` → wrapped in `<RequireAuth>` — redirects to `/sign-in` if no active account
- `RequireAuth` is a small inline guard in `client/App.tsx`

## Sign-in screen (`client/pages/SignInPage.tsx`)
- Full-page centered layout, 448px card, 28px border-radius
- Lists all mock accounts; clicking one calls `signIn(id)` then `navigate("/")`
- Keyboard accessible (tabIndex + Enter)

## Profile menu (`client/components/calendar/ProfileMenu.tsx`)
- Mounted by `TopBar` when `profileMenuOpen === true`
- 360px dropdown, anchored relative to the avatar button
- Sections: current user | other accounts | settings + sign-out | footer links
- Click-outside closes via mousedown listener on document
- Sign out: calls `signOut()` + navigates to `/sign-in`
- Switch account: calls `switchAccount(id)` + closes menu
- Settings: calls `onOpenSettings()` prop (forwarded to TopBar's `setSettingsOpen`)

## TopBar avatar
- Shows `activeAccount.initials` and `activeAccount.color`
- On click: toggles `profileMenuOpen` (local state)
- Open state: 2px primary outline ring + outlineOffset 2
- `aria-label="Account"`, `role="button"`, keyboard-operable
